# 5. EXECUTION STATUS & LIFECYCLE

Implement a consistent execution state machine.

Recommended statuses:

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| pending | Request received and awaiting validation or scheduling |
| validating | Identity, organization, category and permissions are being checked |
| awaiting_approval | Required approval has not yet been granted |
| approved | Required approval has been verified |
| queued | Execution is waiting to start |
| running | Execution is currently in progress |
| completed | Execution completed successfully |
| failed | Execution failed |
| rejected | Request was denied by validation or authorization |
| cancelled | Execution was successfully cancelled |
| timed_out | Execution exceeded its allowed execution time |

Requirements:

- Define valid status transitions.
- Prevent unauthorized or invalid state transitions.
- Record timestamps for status changes.
- Record the reason for rejection, failure, cancellation, or timeout.
- Preserve the complete execution history.
- Do not mark an execution completed before verifying its final result.
- Do not report success when a tool operation failed.
- Do not silently convert failed executions into successful ones.

Use the existing job or queue infrastructure if one already exists.

Do not introduce an unnecessary second queue system.

If background execution infrastructure is required but does not exist, inspect the current stack and propose the smallest compatible implementation.

