# 10. EXECUTION CANCELLATION & TIMEOUTS

Implement controlled cancellation.

Requirements:

- Allow cancellation only to authorized users or systems.
- Verify that the execution belongs to the authorized organization.
- Check whether cancellation is possible in the current state.
- Stop pending or queued executions safely.
- Request cooperative cancellation for running executions.
- Record the cancellation requester, reason and timestamp.
- Do not mark an execution cancelled if the underlying operation has already completed.
- Record operations that completed before cancellation.
- Handle timeouts without silently losing execution state.

Cancellation of an execution must not bypass existing business transaction safety.

